   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Mask Reveal Up\n\nLines reveal upward with a soft masked feel and compact stagger.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A multi-line headline or stacked list needs a clean, contained upward reveal that exits at the end of the clip.\n- A neutral entrance that works across tones: product, editorial, corporate.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The block must hold in place and never exit: use a one-way reveal such as per-character-rise.\n- The reveal should be character-level: use per-character-rise or bottom-up-letters.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Designed to move.\\nBuilt to focus.\"\n- distance (number, 0-120): Distance, default 30\n- font_size (number, 12-160): Font size, default 72\n- color (color): Color, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"600\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Mask Reveal Up\n\n  Lines reveal upward with a soft masked feel and compact stagger.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/mask-reveal-up/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"mask-reveal-up\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    { \"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"Headline lines, one per line break.\", \"default\": \"Designed to move.\\nBuilt to focus.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"distance\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Distance\", \"description\": \"How far below its place each line starts.\", \"default\": 30, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 120, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\" },\n    { \"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Longer text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 72, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 160, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\" },\n    { \"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#171717\" },\n    { \"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"600\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}] }\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Mask Reveal Up</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          color: var(--color, #171717);\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .mru-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          display: flex;\n          align-items: center;\n          justify-content: center;\n        }\n        .mru-block { text-align: center; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1; }\n        .mru-line { display: block; white-space: pre; transform-origin: 50% 50%; opacity: 0; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"mask-reveal-up\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"mru-clip\" class=\"mru-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <span id=\"mru-block\" class=\"mru-block\" role=\"img\"></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function bz(id, a, b, c, d) {\n              return CustomEase.create(\"mru-\" + id, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\");\n            }\n            // interpolate(frame, [a, b], [from, to], { easing }) as a tween (frames at 30 fps).\n            function tw(tl, el, from, to, a, b, ease, keep) {\n              var t = Object.assign({}, to, { duration: (b - a) / 30, ease: ease || \"none\", immediateRender: !keep });\n              tl.fromTo(el, from, t, a / 30);\n            }\n            // Shrink an element's font size so it fits a fraction of the frame width.\n            function fit(el, size, frac) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxWidth = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * frac);\n              if (el.scrollWidth > maxWidth) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (maxWidth / el.scrollWidth));\n                el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            function finish(tl) {\n              if (tl.duration() < TOTAL) tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL - tl.duration() });\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"mask-reveal-up\"] = tl;\n            }\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"Designed to move.\\nBuilt to focus.\");\n            var weight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"600\");\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--color\", vars.color);\n            // interpolate() with clamping, easing given as a function of progress.\n            function ip(f, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (f - a) / (b - a)));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n\n            var distance = num(vars.distance, 30, 0, 120);\n            var block = document.getElementById(\"mru-block\");\n            block.style.fontWeight = weight;\n            var lines = text.split(/\\\\n|\\n/).map(function (l, i) {\n              var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              s.id = \"mru-line-\" + i;\n              s.className = \"mru-line\";\n              s.textContent = l || \" \";\n              block.appendChild(s);\n              return s;\n            });\n            block.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", lines.map(function (l) { return l.textContent; }).join(\" \"));\n            fit(block, num(vars.font_size, 72, 12, 160), 0.9);\n\n            var ENTER = 23, TRAVEL = 11, EXIT = 16, EXIT_FROM = 8, EST = 3, XST = 2;\n            var inE = bz(\"in\", 0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);\n            var outE = bz(\"out\", 0.64, 0, 0.78, 0);\n            var enterEnd = ENTER + (lines.length - 1) * EST;\n            var exitStart = Math.max(enterEnd, TOTAL * 30 - EXIT - (lines.length - 1) * XST);\n            var P = { f: 0 };\n            function apply() {\n              var f = P.f;\n              lines.forEach(function (el, i) {\n                var le = f - i * EST;\n                var lx = f - exitStart - i * XST;\n                var enterP = ip(le, 0, ENTER, 0, 1, inE);\n                var exitP = ip(lx, 0, EXIT, 0, 1, outE);\n                var y = ip(le, 0, TRAVEL, distance, 0, inE) + ip(lx, EXIT_FROM, EXIT, 0, -22, outE);\n                var b = ip(le, 0, ENTER, 6, 0, inE) + ip(lx, 0, EXIT, 0, 6, outE);\n                el.style.opacity = enterP * (1 - exitP);\n                el.style.transform = \"translate(0, \" + y + \"px)\";\n                el.style.filter = b > 0.05 ? \"blur(\" + b + \"px)\" : \"none\";\n              });\n            }\n            apply();\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(P, { f: TOTAL * 30, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: apply }, 0);\n            finish(tl);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
